#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
StarDrive Balance Editor  v.26
------------------------
One window for balancing a StarDrive mod. It reads:
    <mod>\\ShipModules\\*.xml   module stats (cost, mass, power, health...)
    <mod>\\Weapons\\*.xml       weapon stats (damage, range, fire delay...)
    <mod>\\GameText.yaml        names + descriptions (ENG text only)
and joins them: each module row is linked to its weapon (ModuleType's
<WeaponType> == weapon <UID>) and to its name/description text
(<NameIndex>/<DescriptionIndex> == Id in GameText.yaml).

Edit cells (double-click), then Save (Ctrl+S). Only the values you changed are
rewritten, in place - comments, layout, BOM and line endings are untouched.
Before every save the original files are copied to Test Reports and Backups\\<time>\\
and every change is appended to Test Reports and Backups\\changelog.csv.

Handy:
  * Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V in the tables copy / paste cells (several rows at once); right-click any cell or edit box for
    Copy / Paste / Revert / Set to default. Hover for hints. "Revert changes" and "Set to default" buttons on the toolbar.
  * Compare tab: drag a bar / point / icon up or down to change that value (speed list; Shift = finer, Ctrl = coarser).
  * Debug tab: click the Where column to open the file at the right line; many problems have an Auto-fix.
    It also reads the game's blackbox.log (found next to the game, or pick it with "Game log...") and turns the
    warnings / errors in it into suggestions. Anything harmless can be muted with "Ignore".
  * The base game's own textures (.png, or .dds/.tga with Pillow) and GameText are searched too, so modules copied
    from BlackBox / bb+ no longer show as "missing" just because their icon / text lives in the game folder.
  * "Default" = the value before this editor ever changed it (taken from the oldest backup of the file).

Run:  python balance_editor.py            (put it in the mod folder), or
      python balance_editor.py "C:\\Games\\StarDrivePlus64\\Mods\\Star Trek"
Needs only standard Python 3.8+ (tkinter ships with the Windows installer).
"""
